                "entry_id": "a37af6c9-320e-389a-9cc5-a35885c72035",
                "word": "épouvantement",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c176a0c-2ebf-4794-bec4-4213190528b5",
                        "entry_id": "a37af6c9-320e-389a-9cc5-a35885c72035",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "épouvantements"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                        "entry_id": "a37af6c9-320e-389a-9cc5-a35885c72035",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Épouvante portée au plus haut degré."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f95338c9-a249-4f02-b2d0-f470d3c48727",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Les épouvantements de la mort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "950db2ec-edf9-46e7-9cbb-8e3179266238",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Parmi ces dessins qui s’expliquent aisément, il y en a un tout à fait terrible et mystérieux, et dont le sens, vaguement entrevu, est plein de frissons et d’épouvantements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b1143ff-3b0c-4fe2-b6d4-8266e09ba793",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Je me souvenais avec attendrissement quand, le jour de la mort de ma mère, me prenant sur ses genoux, il me dit : « Cela vaut peut-être mieux ainsi. » Et je comprenais aujourd’hui tout ce que cette phrase résumait de douleurs passées et d’épouvantement dans l’avenir."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6825b2a6-8813-402e-ae79-7f1c43c443a0",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Les épouvantements de cette nuit l’avaient réduit au plus complet hébétement, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfb51370-74be-49d6-9862-756504880cbf",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Pourquoi m’avez-vous fait tomber sur cette terre,\nOù, bien qu’aimant sans fin, je reste solitaire\nDans l’épouvantement du sang et des clameurs,\nAlors que par mes bras étendus, par mon cœur,\nPar mes yeux attentifs où l’univers s’amasse,\nPar mon agile esprit qui se nourrit d’espace,\nJ’appartenais à votre ineffable lueur ?…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2e7cdab-3dd0-4cc6-bceb-c20da1120107",
                                "sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                                "text": "Je ne l’ai connue qu’octogénaire, tassée et alourdie par l’âge, allant et venant dans les corridors du Mont-Noir, comme, dans un récit de Walter de la Mare, l’inoubliable tante de Seaton rôde dans sa maison vide, devenue aux yeux des enfants qui la regardent l’épaisse incarnation de la Mort, ou, pis encore, du Mal. Mais le prosaïsme de Noémi ne favorisait pas les épouvantements."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51c73e61-df43-4cc1-bba3-96a8f6f37e62",
                        "source_entry_id": "a37af6c9-320e-389a-9cc5-a35885c72035",
                        "source_sense_id": "804f8cfb-22e9-36d6-8699-20fe23d823d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "fright",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fright",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa1c803c-f91c-3789-b93f-6535abeed209",
                                        "entry_id": "a84ca046-772d-38a0-a762-c37ece529ce9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of terror excited by the sudden appearance of danger; sudden and violent fear, usually of short duration; a sudden alarm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef16aa35-6044-4572-a7aa-b062635474be",
                                                "sense_id": "fa1c803c-f91c-3789-b93f-6535abeed209",
                                                "text": "With a bolt of fright he remembered that there was no bathroom in the Hobhouse Room. He leapt along the corridor in a panic, stopping by the long-case clock at the end where he flattened himself against the wall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73fb4912-def0-387b-adde-d059d2522868",
                                        "entry_id": "a84ca046-772d-38a0-a762-c37ece529ce9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone strange, ugly or shocking, producing a feeling of alarm or aversion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c334c7c-289b-4277-979a-4343acc8282c",
                                                "sense_id": "73fb4912-def0-387b-adde-d059d2522868",
                                                "text": "Her maids were old, and if she took a new one,\nYou might be sure she was a perfect fright;\nShe did this during even her husband's life\nI recommend as much to every wife."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fright",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d51db2ff-e5af-3c9d-a2e9-564b7d548c9b",
                                        "entry_id": "423868ba-6df9-395b-922d-2f4fdb35d3c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To frighten."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a051dd69-5112-4f27-9cd4-c80da5a0d716",
                                                "sense_id": "d51db2ff-e5af-3c9d-a2e9-564b7d548c9b",
                                                "text": "Are not you he […] That frights the maidens of the villagery […] ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afad723d-68bf-4d70-a753-af5695c7594f",
                                                "sense_id": "d51db2ff-e5af-3c9d-a2e9-564b7d548c9b",
                                                "text": "Little Miss Muffet, She sat on a tuffet, Eating of curds and whey; There came a little spider, Who sat down beside her, And frighted Miss Muffet away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42bda33e-0960-4bf0-865d-65f2fdcc04bd",
                                                "sense_id": "d51db2ff-e5af-3c9d-a2e9-564b7d548c9b",
                                                "text": "A very fine situation was proposed to him, where he might have a noble view of the ocean; but he started back, with an attitude of terror Betterton might envy, when Hamlet meets his father's ghost, and cried out,—\"Oh, Christ! the sea looks so fierce that it frights me!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fright",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0460978-d32e-378e-afb4-edb2a6073be4",
                                        "entry_id": "321144ad-81a9-3ff7-9612-0f002b6e1ee7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "frightened; afraid; affright"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aa86401-9323-4005-adb5-86f25c33efc8",
                                                "sense_id": "c0460978-d32e-378e-afb4-edb2a6073be4",
                                                "text": "Don't be fright, it is not so impossible as it seems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44900002-994b-4527-b983-ad32e211ac92",
                                                "sense_id": "c0460978-d32e-378e-afb4-edb2a6073be4",
                                                "text": "Don't be fright, I'm not going to hurt you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a323c9f3-64f8-44fb-a8cc-4d0be5668269",
                                                "sense_id": "c0460978-d32e-378e-afb4-edb2a6073be4",
                                                "text": "He had a great heavy jaw and shoulders like an ox and bore no resemblance to Maurice Leonard. 'Come along, lad,' the sergeant said. 'Come along. Don't be fright. It's what you're here for now, ain't it?'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
